{
 "title": "Variants that carry data",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "In Greengold enum variants can **carry data**, and each variant can carry something different. Such a value is called an \"algebraic data type\". Inside `match` you give names to the data in the pattern."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum Shape:",
    "    Circle(f64)",
    "    Rectangle(f64, f64)",
    "    Point",
    "",
    "fn describe(s: Shape):",
    "    match s:",
    "        Shape.Circle(radius):",
    "            print(\"circle, radius\", radius)",
    "        Shape.Rectangle(w, h):",
    "            print(\"rectangle\", w, \"x\", h)",
    "        Shape.Point:",
    "            print(\"a point\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    describe(Shape.Circle(5.0))",
    "    describe(Shape.Rectangle(10.0, 4.0))",
    "    describe(Shape.Point)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "circle, radius 5",
    "rectangle 10 x 4",
    "a point"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "You can ignore a field you do not care about with `_`: `Shape.Rectangle(w, _):`."
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c06-l02-x1",
   "prompt": "Finish `area(s)`: `w * h` for a rectangle, `side * side` for a square, 0 for `Empty`. Print the area of `Rect(3, 4)`.",
   "starter": [
    "enum Figure:",
    "    Rect(i32, i32)",
    "    Square(i32)",
    "    Empty",
    "",
    "fn area(s: Figure) -> i32:",
    "    match s:",
    "        Figure.Rect(w, h):",
    "            return 0",
    "        Figure.Square(side):",
    "            return 0",
    "        Figure.Empty:",
    "            return 0",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(area(Figure.Rect(3, 4)))"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "enum Figure:",
    "    Rect(i32, i32)",
    "    Square(i32)",
    "    Empty",
    "",
    "fn area(s: Figure) -> i32:",
    "    match s:",
    "        Figure.Rect(w, h):",
    "            return w * h",
    "        Figure.Square(side):",
    "            return side * side",
    "        Figure.Empty:",
    "            return 0",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(area(Figure.Rect(3, 4)))"
   ],
   "hint": "Change the first two `return 0` lines to the calculation.",
   "expected": [
    "12"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c06-l02-q1",
   "q": "In the pattern `Shape.Rectangle(w, _)` what does `_` do?",
   "options": [
    "Ignores the second field",
    "Is an error",
    "Sets the second field to 0"
   ],
   "answer": 0,
   "why": "`_` is the wildcard: that value is not needed."
  }
 ]
}
